==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|frank|ly}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɹæŋkli/}}
* {{hyph|en|frank|ly}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-frankly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# {{lb|en|manner}} In a [[frank]], [[open]] or (too) [[honest]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|He spoke '''frankly''' about the economy.}}
#* {{RQ:Vance Nobody|III}}
#*: She was '''frankly''' disappointed. For some reason she had thought to discover a burglar of one or another accepted type—either a dashing cracksman in full-blown evening dress, lithe, polished, pantherish, or a common yegg, a red-eyed, unshaven burly brute in the rags and tatters of a tramp.
# {{lb|en|sentence adverb}} [[in truth|In truth]], [[to tell the truth]].
#:{{quote-av|en|title=Gone with the Wind|year=1939|actor=Clark Gable|role=Rhett Butler|url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankly,_my_dear,_I_don%27t_give_a_damn|passage='''Frankly''', my dear, I don't give a damn.}}

